[{"id":"MaU_1","ref":"1","section":"Self and consciousness","sa":["ॐ इत्येतदक्षरमिदं सर्वं तस्योपव्याख्यानं","भूतं भवद् भविष्यदिति सर्वमोङ्कार एव","यच्चान्यत् त्रिकालातीतं तदप्योङ्कार एव ॥ १॥"],"iast":["oṃ ityetadakṣaramidaṃ sarvaṃ tasyopavyākhyānaṃ","bhūtaṃ bhavad bhaviṣyaditi sarvamoṅkāra eva","yaccānyat trikālātītaṃ tadapyoṅkāra eva ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"OM is this imperishable Word, OM is the Universe, and this is the exposition of OM. The past, the present and the future, all that was, all that is, all that will be, is OM. Likewise all else that may exist beyond the bounds of Time, that too is OM.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 193","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["ॐ","oṃ","Oṃ, the sacred syllable","oṃ"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["एतत्","etat","this","etat"],["अक्षरम्","akṣaram","syllable","akṣaram"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarvam"],["तस्य","tasya","of that","tasya"],["उपव्याख्यानम्","upavyākhyānam","exposition","upavyākhyānam"],["भूतम्","bhūtam","what has been","bhūtam"],["भवत्","bhavat","what is becoming","bhavat"],["भविष्यत्","bhaviṣyat","what will be","bhaviṣyat"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarvam"],["ओङ्कारः","oṅkāraḥ","the utterance Oṃ","oṅkāraḥ"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["यत्","yat","whatever","yat"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["अन्यत्","anyat","other","anyat"],["त्रिकालातीतम्","trikālātītam","beyond the three times","trikālātītam"],["तत्","tat","that","tat"],["अपि","api","also","api"],["ओङ्कारः","oṅkāraḥ","the utterance Oṃ","oṅkāraḥ"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"]],"tr":{"text":"All this is the letter Om. A vivid explanation of this (is begun). All that is past, present, and future is but Om. Whatever transcends the three periods of time, too, is Om.","by":"Vidyavachaspati V. Panoli","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mandukyopanisad/5.1.mp3","whole":[3.33,27.39]},"hasBhash